  "title": "A grown plane that stops reads the fixed torus's distances, scaled by the growth",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "After the doubling law at every lag for k lags and a stop, for every ring X, contact c and lag T after the stop, c needs X in the stopped run exactly when it does in the fixed (n 2^k x m 2^k)-torus run from an open first row, with or without contacts frozen from the stop on; so the stopped plane reads that torus's cut length, time length and plain first need, its original rings 2^k ring steps apart per original step. Computed: schedules that isolate their rings (P = 3 at g = 2) agree with the fixed torus after a stop; those whose rings hear each other (P = 2, 4 at g = 2 and 3) do not.",
